{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_sign_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_sign_neg","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.lean#L102-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_sign_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_sign_pos","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**T5 sign characterization.** Under the substrate specialization: S > 0\niff |ϑ_K| < |ln q₀| (boost-dominated, muon-type), S < 0 iff |ϑ_K| > |ln q₀|\n(spin-dominated, proton-type). Conditional on A_ω > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_at_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_at_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.lean#L72-L86","doc":"**T5 at substrate: S = A_ω · κ · (ln²q₀ − ϑ²).** For a channel whose\ndeformation map `u` has `Re(u(q₀)) = ln q₀` (`hRe` — an ASSUMPTION on the\nchannel, not a proved fact; see the module docstring) and `Im(u(q₀)) = ϑ` (the\nopen angular deformation), the S-leak becomes the explicit two-parameter\nformula.\n\nThis is the **derive-then-check target**: everything except A_ω and ϑ_K is\nderived from geometry. The T4 crux probe verified that A_ω = 3 + this formula\nreproduces both anchor S values with real ϑ_K. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_expanded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.s_channel_expanded","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaT5Assembly.lean#L62-L70","doc":"**T5 expanded channel formula.** For any `SDeformedVolumeChannel` whose\ncomplex volume is V₄₁, the S-leak expands to `A_ω · κ · (Re²u − Im²u)`.\nThis is the composition of the channel identity with the cusp geometry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}